# World settings

option.WAVING_PLANTS                   = Waving Plants
option.WAVING_PLANTS.comment           = Ground plants wave in the wind.\n\nTo add blocks, edit shaders/block.properties (categories 10016-10018).
option.WAVING_LEAVES                   = Waving Leaves
option.WAVING_LEAVES.comment           = Leaf blocks wave in the wind.\n\nTo add a block to the list of waving leaf blocks, open shaders/block.properties and add it to the relevant category (10019)
option.SLANTED_RAIN                    = Slanted Rain
option.SLANTED_RAIN.comment            = Slanted rain particles. Makes rainy weather a little more atmospheric
option.RAIN_OPACITY                    = Rain Opacity
option.RAIN_OPACITY.comment            = Adjust the opacity of rain particles
option.SNOW_OPACITY                    = Snow Opacity
option.SNOW_OPACITY.comment            = Adjust the opacity of snow particles
option.EDGE_HIGHLIGHT                  = Edge Highlight
option.EDGE_HIGHLIGHT.comment          = Edge highlighting effect inspired by Minecraft Dungeons
option.EDGE_HIGHLIGHT_SCALE            = Edge Highlight Scale
option.EDGE_HIGHLIGHT_SCALE.comment    = Controls the thickness of the edge highlight; change this to match your resource pack resolution
option.MOON_PHASE_AFFECTS_BRIGHTNESS   = Moon Phase Affects Lighting
option.MOON_PHASE_AFFECTS_BRIGHTNESS.comment = Night time brightness is affected by the moon phase
option.DESERT_SANDSTORM                = Desert Sandstorm
option.DESERT_SANDSTORM.comment        = Sandstorm during rain in desert biome
option.END_GLOW                        = End Glow
option.END_GLOW.comment                = Wavery glowing effect in the End. Requires Volumetric Fog
option.END_GLOW_INTENSITY              = End Glow Intensity
option.END_GLOW_INTENSITY.comment      = Adjusts the brightness of the wavy End glow emission. Higher = stronger glow; 0 disables the emission visually while keeping the toggle.

# Weather
option.RANDOM_WEATHER_VARIATION            = Random Variation
option.RANDOM_WEATHER_VARIATION.comment = Drifts temperature, humidity, wind and turbulence over time so weather evolves on its own.
option.BIOME_WEATHER_VARIATION             = Biome-based Variation
option.BIOME_WEATHER_VARIATION.comment = Lets the current biome shape the weather, so deserts stay dry and jungles stay humid.
option.WEATHER_TEMPERATURE_BIAS            = Temperature Bias
option.WEATHER_TEMPERATURE_BIAS.comment = Shifts the baseline temperature. Warmer skies grow taller clouds, colder skies flatten them out.
option.WEATHER_HUMIDITY_BIAS               = Humidity Bias
option.WEATHER_HUMIDITY_BIAS.comment = Shifts baseline moisture. Higher values thicken cloud cover, lower values clear the sky.
option.WEATHER_WIND_BIAS                   = Windiness Bias
option.WEATHER_WIND_BIAS.comment = Shifts the baseline wind strength, speeding up or calming cloud drift.
option.WEATHER_TURBULENCE_BIAS             = Turbulence Bias
option.WEATHER_TURBULENCE_BIAS.comment = Shifts baseline turbulence. Higher values tear clouds into broken, wispy detail.
option.WEATHER_TEMPERATURE_VARIATION_SPEED = Temperature Variation Speed
option.WEATHER_TEMPERATURE_VARIATION_SPEED.comment = How fast temperature drifts. Higher values make cloud shapes evolve more quickly.
option.WEATHER_HUMIDITY_VARIATION_SPEED    = Humidity Variation Speed
option.WEATHER_HUMIDITY_VARIATION_SPEED.comment = How fast moisture drifts. Higher values make cloud cover build and break faster.
option.WEATHER_WIND_VARIATION_SPEED        = Windiness Variation Speed
option.WEATHER_WIND_VARIATION_SPEED.comment = How fast wind strength drifts. Higher values make gusts come and go faster.
option.WEATHER_TURBULENCE_VARIATION_SPEED  = Turbulence Variation Speed
option.WEATHER_TURBULENCE_VARIATION_SPEED.comment = How fast turbulence drifts. Higher values make cloud detail churn faster.

# Lighting settings

option.AO_IN_SUNLIGHT                  = AO in Sunlight
option.AO_IN_SUNLIGHT.comment          = Whether to apply shader ambient occlusion in direct sunlight/moonlight
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS                   = Cloud Shadows
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS.comment           = Shadows cast by clouds on the ground
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS_INTENSITY         = Cloud Shadows Intensity
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS_INTENSITY.comment = Adjusts the intensity of cloud shadows
option.SSS_SHEEN                       = SSS Sheen
option.SSS_SHEEN.comment               = Specular "sheen" effect on plants and leaves, helps tall grass and stuff to blend better with the grass specular
option.SSS_INTENSITY                   = SSS Intensity
option.SSS_INTENSITY.comment           = Adjusts the brightness of subsurface scattering (SSS)
option.SHADING_STRENGTH                = Shading Strength
option.SHADING_STRENGTH.comment        = Direct-light shading contrast. Lower brightens faces turned away from the sun; higher deepens them.

option.SHADOW                          = Shadow Mapping
option.SHADOW.comment = Enables shadows cast by the sun and moon onto the world. Disable for maximum performance — no shadows will be rendered.
option.SHADOW_PCF                      = Shadowmap Filtering
option.SHADOW_PCF.comment = Softens shadow edges using percentage-closer filtering. When enabled, shadows look smoother and less pixelated.
option.SHADOW_PCF_STEPS_SCALE            = Filter Quality
option.SHADOW_PCF_STEPS_SCALE.comment    = Scales how many filter taps the shadowmap filtering uses. Higher = smoother, less noisy soft shadows at higher GPU cost.
option.SHADOW_SSRT                     = Distant Shadows
option.SHADOW_SSRT.comment = Extends shadows beyond the shadow map distance using screen-space ray tracing. Fills in far shadows without increasing shadow map size. Moderate performance cost.
option.SHADOW_SSRT_STEPS               = Distant Shadow Quality
option.SHADOW_SSRT_STEPS.comment = Adjusts the number of ray steps for screen-space distant shadows. Higher = more accurate, less noisy far shadows at higher GPU cost.
option.SHADOW_COLOR                    = Colored Shadows
option.SHADOW_COLOR.comment            = Translucent blocks cast tinted shadows
option.SHADOW_COLOR_INTENSITY            = Tint Strength
option.SHADOW_COLOR_INTENSITY.comment    = Adjusts how strongly translucent blocks tint the shadows behind them. Higher = deeper, more saturated color bleed; 0 = plain white shadows.
option.SHADOW_VPS                      = Variable Penumbra Shadows
option.SHADOW_VPS.comment              = Shadows grow softer further from their caster
option.shadowMapResolution             = Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment = Adjusts the size of the shadow map texture. Higher = sharper, more detailed shadows at higher VRAM and GPU cost.
option.shadowDistance                  = Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment = Maximum distance shadows are rendered, in blocks. Higher values show shadows farther away but reduce detail per block and increase cost.
option.sunPathRotation                 = Sun Path Tilt
option.sunPathRotation.comment = Tilts the sun and moon path across the sky in degrees. Negative values tilt south. Affects time-of-day lighting direction.
option.SHADOW_PENUMBRA_SCALE           = Shadow Softness
option.SHADOW_PENUMBRA_SCALE.comment   = Scales the overall softness of all shadows. Lower = sharper hard shadows, higher = larger, softer penumbras.
option.ENTITY_SHADOWS                  = Entity Shadows
option.ENTITY_SHADOWS.comment          = When enabled, living entities and dropped items cast shadows.\nDisable to improve performance in survival bases with large farms.
option.BLOCK_ENTITY_SHADOWS            = Block Entity Shadows
option.BLOCK_ENTITY_SHADOWS.comment = When enabled, chests, signs, banners and other block entities cast shadows. Lower cost than full entity shadows.
option.PIXELATED_SHADOWS               = Pixelated Shadows
option.PIXELATED_SHADOWS.comment       = Shadows snap to the block texel grid, creating a retro pixelated look. For stylistic screenshots.
option.PIXELATED_SHADOWS_RESOLUTION    = Pixel Size
option.PIXELATED_SHADOWS_RESOLUTION.comment = Adjusts the texel grid size for pixelated shadows. Lower = chunkier, more blocky pixels.
option.SSS_STEPS                       = SSS Steps 
option.SSS_STEPS.comment               = Increase to reduce noise on foliage and other materials with SSS, at the cost of performance.

option.SHADER_AO                       = Shader AO
option.SHADER_AO.comment               = AO method. Off - no shader AO. SSAO - screen-space, light. GTAO - horizon-based, better quality; provides the bent normal used by SSPT
value.SHADER_AO.SHADER_AO_NONE         = Off
value.SHADER_AO.SHADER_AO_SSAO         = SSAO
value.SHADER_AO.SHADER_AO_GTAO         = GTAO
option.VANILLA_AO                      = Vanilla AO
option.VANILLA_AO.comment              = Minecraft's built-in ambient occlusion
option.H_BASIS_SKYLIGHT                = H-Basis Skylight
option.H_BASIS_SKYLIGHT.comment        = Directional sky ambient from a live H-basis projection of the sky map. Off falls back to the flat sky average.
option.H_BASIS_INTENSITY               = Ambient Intensity
option.H_BASIS_INTENSITY.comment       = Master brightness of directional sky ambient. Higher = brighter sky fill.
option.H_BASIS_SKY_SAMPLES             = Projection Samples
option.H_BASIS_SKY_SAMPLES.comment     = Sky directions sampled per frame for the H-basis projection. Higher = smoother, more accurate ambient at higher cost.
option.VANILLA_AO_INTENSITY            = Vanilla AO Intensity
option.VANILLA_AO_INTENSITY.comment    = Strength of vanilla ambient occlusion. Softened automatically while a shader AO method is active, so corners never double-darken.
option.VANILLA_AO_LIFT                   = Vanilla AO Lift
option.VANILLA_AO_LIFT.comment           = Lifts the darkest vanilla AO shadows toward flat lighting. Higher = shallower, more washed-out crevices; 0 = full-depth vanilla AO.
option.SSAO_STEPS                        = SSAO Samples
option.SSAO_STEPS.comment                = Sample count for screen-space ambient occlusion. Higher = smoother, less noisy AO at higher GPU cost.
option.SSAO_RADIUS                       = SSAO Radius
option.SSAO_RADIUS.comment               = Occlusion radius for screen-space AO in blocks. Larger = wider, softer contact shadows.
option.GTAO_RADIUS                       = GTAO Radius
option.GTAO_RADIUS.comment               = Occlusion radius for horizon-based AO in blocks. Larger = wider, softer crevice shading.
option.GTAO_HORIZON_STEPS                = GTAO Horizon Steps
option.GTAO_HORIZON_STEPS.comment        = Steps per horizon line for GTAO. Higher = more accurate horizon search at higher GPU cost.

option.SUN_NR                          = §c▍ §fRed — Noon
option.SUN_NR.comment = Adjusts the red tint of sunlight at noon. Higher = warmer midday sun.
option.SUN_NG                          = §a▍ §fGreen — Noon
option.SUN_NG.comment = Adjusts the green tint of sunlight at noon. Higher = less pink, more neutral daylight.
option.SUN_NB                          = §9▍ §fBlue — Noon
option.SUN_NB.comment = Adjusts the blue tint of sunlight at noon. Higher = cooler, more bluish midday light.
option.SUN_MR                          = §c▍ §fRed — Morning
option.SUN_MR.comment = Adjusts the red tint of sunlight at sunrise. Higher = warmer, redder dawn light.
option.SUN_MG                          = §a▍ §fGreen — Morning
option.SUN_MG.comment = Adjusts the green tint of sunlight at sunrise. Affects the balance between orange and yellow dawn.
option.SUN_MB                          = §9▍ §fBlue — Morning
option.SUN_MB.comment = Adjusts the blue tint of sunlight at sunrise. Higher = less orange, more neutral morning.
option.SUN_ER                          = §c▍ §fRed — Evening
option.SUN_ER.comment = Adjusts the red tint of sunlight at sunset. Higher = warmer, redder dusk light.
option.SUN_EG                          = §a▍ §fGreen — Evening
option.SUN_EG.comment = Adjusts the green tint of sunlight at sunset. Affects the balance between orange and yellow dusk.
option.SUN_EB                          = §9▍ §fBlue — Evening
option.SUN_EB.comment = Adjusts the blue tint of sunlight at sunset. Higher = cooler, less orange evening light.
option.MOON_R                          = §c▍ §fRed — Moonlight
option.MOON_R.comment = Adjusts the red tint of moonlight. Higher = warmer night light.
option.MOON_G                          = §a▍ §fGreen — Moonlight
option.MOON_G.comment = Adjusts the green tint of moonlight. Affects the coolness of night lighting.
option.MOON_B                          = §9▍ §fBlue — Moonlight
option.MOON_B.comment = Adjusts the blue tint of moonlight. Higher = cooler, more bluish nights.
option.LIGHTNING_FLASH                 = Lightning Flash
option.LIGHTNING_FLASH.comment = Controls lightning flash.
option.NETHER_USE_BIOME_COLOR          = Use Biome Color
option.NETHER_USE_BIOME_COLOR.comment = When enabled, Nether fog and ambient color adapts to the current biome. When disabled, uses the static color below.
option.NETHER_I                        = Nether Fog Intensity
option.NETHER_I.comment = Adjusts the overall brightness of Nether fog and ambient light. Higher = brighter, more washed-out Nether.
option.NETHER_S                        = Nether Fog Saturation
option.NETHER_S.comment = Adjusts the color vividness of Nether fog. Higher = more saturated orange/red, lower = more grey.
option.NETHER_R                        = §c▍ §fRed — Nether
option.NETHER_R.comment = Adjusts the red tint of the static Nether ambient color (when Use Biome Color is off).
option.NETHER_G                        = §a▍ §fGreen — Nether
option.NETHER_G.comment = Adjusts the green tint of the static Nether ambient color. Affects the orange-to-yellow balance.
option.NETHER_B                        = §9▍ §fBlue — Nether
option.NETHER_B.comment = Adjusts the blue tint of the static Nether ambient color. Higher = more purple/cooler Nether.
option.END_LIGHT_R                     = §c▍ §fRed — End Light
option.END_LIGHT_R.comment = Adjusts the red tint of direct light in the End (from the central light source).
option.END_LIGHT_G                     = §a▍ §fGreen — End Light
option.END_LIGHT_G.comment = Adjusts the green tint of direct light in the End.
option.END_LIGHT_B                     = §9▍ §fBlue — End Light
option.END_LIGHT_B.comment = Adjusts the blue tint of direct light in the End. Higher = cooler, more bluish End light.
option.END_LIGHT_I                     = End Direct Intensity
option.END_LIGHT_I.comment = Adjusts the brightness of direct light in the End. Higher = stronger highlights from the End light source.
option.END_AMBIENT_R                   = §c▍ §fRed — End Ambient
option.END_AMBIENT_R.comment = Adjusts the red tint of ambient skylight in the End.
option.END_AMBIENT_G                   = §a▍ §fGreen — End Ambient
option.END_AMBIENT_G.comment = Adjusts the green tint of ambient skylight in the End.
option.END_AMBIENT_B                   = §9▍ §fBlue — End Ambient
option.END_AMBIENT_B.comment = Adjusts the blue tint of ambient skylight in the End. Higher = more violet/blue ambient.
option.END_AMBIENT_I                   = End Ambient Intensity
option.END_AMBIENT_I.comment = Adjusts the brightness of ambient skylight in the End. Higher = less contrast, more evenly lit.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_R                    = §c▍ §fRed — Block Light
option.BLOCKLIGHT_R.comment = Adjusts the red tint of artificial block lights (torches, lanterns, glowstone). Higher = warmer block light.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_G                    = §a▍ §fGreen — Block Light
option.BLOCKLIGHT_G.comment = Adjusts the green tint of block lights. Affects the orange-to-yellow balance of torch light.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_B                    = §9▍ §fBlue — Block Light
option.BLOCKLIGHT_B.comment = Adjusts the blue tint of block lights. Higher = cooler, whiter light.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_I                    = Block Light Intensity
option.BLOCKLIGHT_I.comment = Adjusts the overall brightness of block light sources. Higher = stronger torch and lamp illumination.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_TEMPERATURE          = Block Light Temperature
option.BLOCKLIGHT_TEMPERATURE.comment = Blackbody temperature of block lights in Kelvin. Lower is warmer candle glow, higher is cooler white. Neutral at 3400K.
option.CAVE_LIGHTING_I                  = Cave Ambient
option.CAVE_LIGHTING_I.comment = Adjusts the base brightness of underground ambient light when no direct light is present. Higher = caves appear less pitch-black.




