# Sky settings

option.VANILLA_SUN                     = Sun Texture
option.VANILLA_SUN.comment = When enabled, shows Minecraft's default sun texture. When disabled, uses the shader's procedural sun disc.
option.VANILLA_MOON                    = Moon Texture
option.VANILLA_MOON.comment = When enabled, shows Minecraft's default moon texture. When disabled, uses the shader's procedural moon disc.
option.SUN_ANGULAR_RADIUS              = Sun Size
option.SUN_ANGULAR_RADIUS.comment = Adjusts the apparent size of the sun disc in the sky. Larger = bigger sun and softer shadows due to larger light source.
option.MOON_ANGULAR_RADIUS             = Moon Size
option.MOON_ANGULAR_RADIUS.comment = Adjusts the apparent size of the moon disc at night. Larger = bigger moon and softer moon shadows.
option.PLANET_BOUNCE                   = Planet Bounce Light
option.PLANET_BOUNCE.comment           = Ground-bounced sun and moonlight re-scattered through the air. Warms the horizon and downward views almost for free.
option.STARS                           = Stars
option.STARS.comment                   = Stars in the night sky. Low performance impact
option.STARS_INTENSITY                 = Intensity
option.STARS_INTENSITY.comment         = Controls the brightness of stars in the night sky
option.STARS_COVERAGE                  = Coverage
option.STARS_COVERAGE.comment          = Controls the number of stars in the night sky
option.GALAXY                          = Galaxy
option.GALAXY.comment                  = Galaxy image in the night sky
option.GALAXY_INTENSITY                = Galaxy Intensity
option.GALAXY_INTENSITY.comment        = Controls the brightness of the galaxy in the night sky
option.CREPUSCULAR_RAYS                = Crepuscular Rays
option.CREPUSCULAR_RAYS.comment = Enables god rays (light shafts) visible when the sun is near the horizon through fog and clouds. Best seen at sunrise/sunset.
option.CREPUSCULAR_RAYS_INTENSITY      = Ray Intensity
option.CREPUSCULAR_RAYS_INTENSITY.comment = Adjusts the brightness and contrast of god rays. Higher = more visible light shafts.
option.CREPUSCULAR_RAYS_STEPS_HORIZON  = Horizon Quality
option.CREPUSCULAR_RAYS_STEPS_HORIZON.comment = Adjusts ray-marching quality toward the horizon. Higher = smoother, more accurate rays at higher GPU cost.
option.CREPUSCULAR_RAYS_STEPS_ZENITH   = Zenith Quality
option.CREPUSCULAR_RAYS_STEPS_ZENITH.comment = Adjusts ray-marching quality toward the zenith (straight up). Higher = smoother rays overhead at higher cost.
option.LIGHTNING_FLASH                 = Lightning Flash
option.RAINBOWS                        = Rainbows
option.RAINBOWS.comment = When enabled, a faint rainbow appears opposite the sun during and just after rain.
option.END_SUN_EFFECT                  = End Sun Effect
option.END_SUN_EFFECT.comment = Controls end sun effect.
option.ATMOSPHERE_SATURATION_BOOST                    = Atmosphere Saturation Boost
option.ATMOSPHERE_SATURATION_BOOST.comment            = Increases the saturation of the sky and sunlight color depending on the time of day
option.ATMOSPHERE_SATURATION_BOOST_INTENSITY          = Saturation Boost Intensity
option.ATMOSPHERE_SATURATION_BOOST_INTENSITY.comment  = Adjust the intensity of Atmosphere Saturation Boost
option.ATMOSPHERE_RAIN_DESATURATION                   = Atmosphere Rain Desaturation
option.ATMOSPHERE_RAIN_DESATURATION.comment           = Desaturates the atmosphere during rain, making for colder looking rain
option.ATMOSPHERE_RAIN_DESATURATION_INTENSITY         = Desaturation Intensity
option.ATMOSPHERE_RAIN_DESATURATION_INTENSITY.comment = Adjust the intensity of Atmosphere Rain Desaturation

# Clouds
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS                       = Cumulus Clouds
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS.comment               = Low-altitude volumetric clouds designed to resemble cumulus clouds. Adds depth and atmosphere to the sky. Performance impact varies with cloud density.
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_PRIMARY_STEPS_H       = Primary Steps - Horizon
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_PRIMARY_STEPS_H.comment = Ray-march steps toward the horizon for cumulus. Higher = more accurate horizon clouds at higher GPU cost.
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_PRIMARY_STEPS_Z       = Primary Steps - Zenith
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_PRIMARY_STEPS_Z.comment = Ray-march steps toward the zenith for cumulus. Higher = more accurate overhead clouds at higher cost.
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_LIGHTING_STEPS        = Lighting Steps
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_LIGHTING_STEPS.comment = Shadow/light sampling steps inside cumulus clouds. Higher = softer, more accurate scattering.
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_AMBIENT_STEPS         = Ambient Steps
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_AMBIENT_STEPS.comment = Ambient occlusion sampling steps for cumulus. Higher = better self-shadowing.
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_ALTITUDE              = Altitude
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_ALTITUDE.comment = Controls altitude.
suffix.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_ALTITUDE              = m
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_THICKNESS             = Thickness
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_THICKNESS.comment = Controls thickness.
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_DENSITY               = Density
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_DENSITY.comment = Controls density.
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_COVERAGE              = Coverage
option.CLOUDS_CUMULUS_COVERAGE.comment = Controls coverage.
