# Fog settings

option.BORDER_FOG                           = Border Fog
option.BORDER_FOG.comment                   = Thick fog that extends to the edges of the render distance. Helps hide chunk borders and creates a more seamless transition to the void.
option.CAVE_FOG                             = Cave Fog
option.CAVE_FOG.comment                     = Faint glowing fog underground. Lifts cave interiors with minimal cost.
option.BLOOMY_FOG                           = Bloomy Fog
option.BLOOMY_FOG.comment                   = Strong bloom inside fog volumes, simulating scattered light from bright objects, including behind them. Cheap.
option.BLOOMY_FOG_INTENSITY                 = Bloomy Fog Intensity
option.BLOOMY_FOG_INTENSITY.comment         = Adjusts the intensity of "bloomy fog"
option.OVERWORLD_FOG_INTENSITY              = Overworld Fog Intensity
option.OVERWORLD_FOG_INTENSITY.comment    = Controls the intensity of overworld fog. Higher values create denser fog near the ground, lower values make fog thinner.

value.MIST_MODE.MIST_MODE_OFF              = Off
value.MIST_MODE.MIST_MODE_BASIC            = Basic
value.MIST_MODE.MIST_MODE_ADVANCED         = Advanced
option.MIST_MODE                           = Ground Mist
option.MIST_MODE.comment                  = Ground-hugging haze. Basic is cheap noise mist; Advanced adds sun self-shadowing with cloud occlusion at higher cost.
option.MIST_MODE_OFF                       = Off
option.MIST_MODE_BASIC                     = Basic
option.MIST_MODE_ADVANCED                  = Advanced
option.MIST_DENSITY                        = Mist Density
option.MIST_DENSITY.comment               = Overall thickness of the mist layer. Higher values produce denser, more opaque ground fog.
option.MIST_COLOR_R                       = §c▍ §fRed — Mist
option.MIST_COLOR_R.comment               = Red tint of ground mist over its time-of-day hue. 1.00 is neutral; lower cools, higher warms.
option.MIST_COLOR_G                       = §a▍ §fGreen — Mist
option.MIST_COLOR_G.comment               = Green tint of ground mist. Multiplies the mist's time-of-day hue; 1.00 leaves it unchanged.
option.MIST_COLOR_B                       = §9▍ §fBlue — Mist
option.MIST_COLOR_B.comment               = Blue tint of ground mist. Multiplies the mist's time-of-day hue; 1.00 leaves it unchanged, higher values push it cooler.
option.MIST_ALTITUDE                       = Mist Ceiling
option.MIST_ALTITUDE.comment              = Maximum altitude (blocks) above which mist cannot exist. Lower values keep mist close to the ground.
option.MIST_FALLOFF_RATE                   = Mist Falloff Rate
option.MIST_FALLOFF_RATE.comment          = How quickly mist thins with altitude above sea level. Higher = thinner layer, lower = mist reaches higher.
option.MIST_SEA_LEVEL_BIAS                 = Mist Sea Level Bias
option.MIST_SEA_LEVEL_BIAS.comment        = Shifts the mist base up or down relative to the configured sea level. Positive = mist starts higher, negative = mist starts lower.
option.MIST_SHADOW_STEPS                   = Mist Shadow Steps
option.MIST_SHADOW_STEPS.comment          = Number of ray-march steps toward the sun for mist self-shadowing (Advanced mode only). Higher = more accurate self-shadowing at higher GPU cost.
option.MIST_SHADOW_STEP_LENGTH                = Mist Shadow Step Length
option.MIST_SHADOW_STEP_LENGTH.comment        = Distance in blocks between mist self-shadow samples (Advanced mode only). Smaller steps are more accurate but cover a shorter range (range = steps x length); larger steps reach further but can look coarse.
option.OZONE_LAYER                         = Ozone Absorption Layer
option.OZONE_LAYER.comment = Adjustable stratospheric ozone layer. Tints sunlight, sky, fog and bounce, most visibly at dawn and dusk.
option.OZONE_AMOUNT                        = Ozone Amount
option.OZONE_AMOUNT.comment = Strength of the ozone layer. 1.00 is a natural column; higher values deepen the twilight blue zenith and redden horizon light; 0 disables the absorption.
option.OZONE_COLOR_R                      = §c▍ §fRed — Ozone
option.OZONE_COLOR_R.comment              = Ozone absorption of red light. 1.00 is natural; higher removes more red from twilight, lower lets more through.
option.OZONE_COLOR_G                      = §a▍ §fGreen — Ozone
option.OZONE_COLOR_G.comment              = How strongly the ozone layer absorbs green light. Green is the strongest absorption band, so this has the biggest effect on the twilight hue.
option.OZONE_COLOR_B                      = §9▍ §fBlue — Ozone
option.OZONE_COLOR_B.comment              = How strongly the ozone layer absorbs blue light. 1.00 is the natural spectrum; raising it dulls the twilight blue.
option.OZONE_ALTITUDE                      = Ozone Layer Altitude
option.OZONE_ALTITUDE.comment = Peak altitude of the ozone layer in kilometres. The real layer peaks around 20-30km; higher layers saturate less at the horizon.
option.OZONE_THICKNESS                     = Ozone Layer Thickness
option.OZONE_THICKNESS.comment = Thickness of the layer in kilometres. Thin layers concentrate absorption and amplify horizon-grazing paths; thick layers spread it out.
option.OZONE_SKY                           = Ozone Sky Absorption
option.OZONE_SKY.comment = Applies the ozone layer to the sky: view- and light-path absorption on the atmosphere, deepening the twilight blue zenith and warming horizon light.
option.OZONE_FOG                           = Ozone Fog Scattering
option.OZONE_FOG.comment = Applies the ozone layer to air fog: an ozone-aware multiple scattering approximation where higher scatter orders lose more green/red to the ozone bands.
option.OZONE_MIST                          = Ozone Mist Tint
option.OZONE_MIST.comment = Applies the ozone layer to ground mist: near dawn and dusk the mist tint picks up the ozone-filtered twilight spectrum.
option.OZONE_PLANET_BOUNCE                 = Ozone Planet Bounce
option.OZONE_PLANET_BOUNCE.comment = Applies the ozone layer to planet bounce light: ground-bounced light is filtered through the ozone layer again on its way back up into the sky.
option.SANDSTORM_LAYER                     = Sandstorm Sky Layer
option.SANDSTORM_LAYER.comment = Dust-dimmed direct sun and moonlight during desert storms. Follows the live storm amount.
option.SANDSTORM_SKY                       = Sandstorm Sky Scattering
option.SANDSTORM_SKY.comment = Dusty sky during desert storms. Hazes the horizon and dims the sun disk to match the fog.
option.SANDSTORM_MIST                      = Sandstorm Mist Tint
option.SANDSTORM_MIST.comment = Applies the desert sandstorm to ground mist: while a storm is active the mist tint blends toward the warm dust spectrum.
option.SANDSTORM_BOUNCE                    = Sandstorm Planet Bounce
option.SANDSTORM_BOUNCE.comment = Applies the desert sandstorm to planet bounce light: ground-bounced light is re-filtered through the dust layer on its way back up into the sky.
option.VL                                   = Volumetric Fog
option.VL.comment                           = Adds volumetric fog with light shafts and variable density. Creates atmosphere and sun rays streaming through the fog. Requires significant GPU resources.
option.VL_RENDER_SCALE                      = VL Render Scale
option.VL_RENDER_SCALE.comment = Controls vl render scale.
option.AIR_FOG_CLOUDY_NOISE                 = Cloudy Fog
option.AIR_FOG_CLOUDY_NOISE.comment         = Subtle cloud-like shapes within the fog, best visible in morning light. Requires volumetric fog to be enabled for the effect to appear.
option.AIR_FOG_COLORED_LIGHT_SHAFTS         = Colored Light Shafts
option.AIR_FOG_COLORED_LIGHT_SHAFTS.comment    = Sun shafts tinted by the glass or leaves they pass through. Produces colored god rays.
option.AIR_FOG_COLORED_LIGHT_SHAFTS_INTENSITY         = Colored Light Shafts Intensity
option.AIR_FOG_COLORED_LIGHT_SHAFTS_INTENSITY.comment = Controls the strength of the color tinting applied to light shafts


