option.AIR_FOG_MIE_DENSITY_NOON              = Noon Density
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_DENSITY_NOON.comment = Controls noon density.
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_DENSITY_EVENING           = Evening Density
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_DENSITY_EVENING.comment = Controls evening density.
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_DENSITY_MIDNIGHT          = Midnight Density
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_DENSITY_MIDNIGHT.comment = Controls midnight density.
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_DENSITY_RAIN              = Rain Density
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_DENSITY_RAIN.comment = Controls rain density.
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_DENSITY_BLUE_HOUR         = Dawn/Dusk Density
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_DENSITY_BLUE_HOUR.comment = Controls dawn/dusk density.
option.MIE_ANISOTROPY                     = Sky Mie Anisotropy
option.MIE_ANISOTROPY.comment             = Mie scattering directionality. Higher concentrates the haze glow around sun and moon; lower spreads it. Default 0.77.
option.FOG_MIE_ANISOTROPY                 = Fog Mie Anisotropy
option.FOG_MIE_ANISOTROPY.comment         = Forward-scattering strength of fog. Higher glows toward sun and moon; 0 scatters evenly. Default 0.50.
option.MIE_COLOR_R                        = §c▍ §fRed — Mie
option.MIE_COLOR_R.comment                = Red tint of Mie scattering (sky haze and air fog). 1.00 is the physical value; lowering it removes red from the haze, raising it warms it.
option.MIE_COLOR_G                        = §a▍ §fGreen — Mie
option.MIE_COLOR_G.comment                = Green tint of Mie scattering (sky haze and air fog). 1.00 is the physical value.
option.MIE_COLOR_B                        = §9▍ §fBlue — Mie
option.MIE_COLOR_B.comment                = Blue tint of Mie scattering (sky haze and air fog). 1.00 is the physical value; raising it cools the haze.
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_FALLOFF_START             = Altitude Fade Start
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_FALLOFF_START.comment     = Altitude above sea level at which the mie fog begins to decrease
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_FALLOFF_HALF_LIFE         = Altitude Fade Half Life
option.AIR_FOG_MIE_FALLOFF_HALF_LIFE.comment = Altitude above the Mie Falloff Start where the mie fog density is halved


# Materials settings

option.NORMAL_MAPPING                  = Normal Mapping
option.NORMAL_MAPPING.comment          = Whether to use normal maps from the resource pack. Enable for PBR packs to see proper surface detail. Disable for compatibility or performance.
option.SPECULAR_MAPPING                = Specular Mapping
option.SPECULAR_MAPPING.comment        = Whether to use specular maps from the resource pack. Enable for PBR packs to see proper metallic/specular highlights. Disable for compatibility or performance.
option.POM                             = Parallax Occlusion Mapping
option.POM.comment = Parallax occlusion mapping: offsets texture coordinates for real surface depth. Heavy on weaker GPUs.
option.POM_SHADOW                    = POM Self-Shadowing
option.POM_SLOPE_NORMALS               = Slope Normals
option.POM_SLOPE_NORMALS.comment       = Uses the POM height field gradient to add relief-aware surface normals to lighting. Disable to keep the underlying normal map unchanged.
option.POM_DEPTH_WRITE              = Depth Write
option.POM_DEPTH_WRITE.comment      = Writes POM relief into the depth buffer so sunlight, skylight and SSPT respect surface height. Disable for compatibility or speed.
option.POM_SHADOW.comment            = Adds self-shadowing inside the POM height field from the main light direction. Higher sample counts improve quality at a performance cost.
option.TEXTURE_FORMAT                  = Texture Format
option.TEXTURE_FORMAT.comment          = The texture format used by the resource pack. Most modern resource packs use lab_p_b_r, while packs that are designed to work with SEUS may use OldPBR.
option.HARDCODED_SPECULAR              = Hardcoded Specular
option.HARDCODED_SPECULAR.comment      = Hardcoded specular reflections for metallic blocks. Uses built-in values for metal-like surfaces instead of resource pack specular maps.
option.HARDCODED_EMISSION              = Hardcoded Emission
option.HARDCODED_EMISSION.comment      = Hardcoded emission for blocks like torches and glowstone. Provides built-in emissive lighting without requiring resource pack textures.
option.GLOBAL_EMISSION_CURVE=Emission Curve
option.GLOBAL_EMISSION_CURVE.comment=Reshapes emission response (1.0 = neutral). Lower lifts dim glow, higher crushes it toward bright cores.
option.GLOBAL_EMISSION_INTENSITY=Emission Intensity
option.GLOBAL_EMISSION_INTENSITY.comment=Overall emissive brightness after the curve is applied.
option.HARDCODED_SSS                   = Hardcoded SSS
option.HARDCODED_SSS.comment           = Hardcoded subsurface scattering for organic blocks like leaves and wax. Uses built-in scattering profiles instead of resource pack maps.
option.RAIN_PUDDLES                    = Rain Puddles
option.RAIN_PUDDLES.comment            = Controls rain puddles on the ground. Puddles form on flat surfaces exposed to open sky while it's raining, in biomes wet enough to actually rain.
option.EMISSION_STRENGTH               = Emission Strength
option.EMISSION_STRENGTH.comment       = Brightness of emissive blocks such as torches, including their light glow. Also affects hardcoded emissives.
option.DIRECTIONAL_LIGHTMAPS           = Directional Lightmaps
option.DIRECTIONAL_LIGHTMAPS.comment   = Blocklight and skylight follow surface normals for deeper contact shading. May artifact at sharp lightmap gradients.
option.DIRECTIONAL_LIGHTMAPS_INTENSITY = Directional Lightmaps Strength
option.DIRECTIONAL_LIGHTMAPS_INTENSITY.comment = Adjusts the intensity of Directional Lightmaps
option.POM_DEPTH                       = Parallax Depth
option.POM_DEPTH.comment               = Controls how deeply POM recesses into block geometry. Higher values increase the parallax effect but may reduce performance.
option.POM_SAMPLES                     = Parallax Samples
option.POM_SHADOW_SAMPLES              = POM Self-Shadow Samples
option.POM_SHADOW_SAMPLES.comment      = Controls the number of height-field samples used for POM self-shadowing. Higher values improve detail but cost more performance.
option.POM_SAMPLES.comment             = Adjusts the number of sampling steps for POM. Higher values increase quality and reduce noise but significantly impact performance.
option.POM_DISTANCE                    = POM Distance
option.POM_DISTANCE.comment            = Controls the maximum distance at which POM is calculated. Objects beyond this distance use standard texture coordinates. Decreasing can improve performance.
option.REFRACTION                      = Refraction
option.REFRACTION.comment = Selects the refraction mode or method.
value.REFRACTION.REFRACTION_OFF        = Off
value.REFRACTION.REFRACTION_ALL        = Everything
value.REFRACTION.REFRACTION_WATER_ONLY = Water Only
option.REFRACTION_INTENSITY            = Refraction Intensity
option.REFRACTION_INTENSITY.comment    = Adjusts the intensity of refractions on water
option.REFRACTION_DISPERSION_INTENSITY         = Refraction Dispersion
option.REFRACTION_DISPERSION_INTENSITY.comment = Adds chromatic dispersion (RGB fringing) to refracted water/glass, like light splitting through a prism

suffix.POM_DEPTH                       = m
suffix.POM_DISTANCE                    = m

value.TEXTURE_FORMAT.TEXTURE_FORMAT_LAB = labPBR
value.TEXTURE_FORMAT.TEXTURE_FORMAT_OLD = Old PBR

option.ENVIRONMENT_REFLECTIONS         = Environment Reflections
option.ENVIRONMENT_REFLECTIONS.comment    = Screen-space reflections on water and shiny blocks. Heavy on weaker GPUs.
option.SKY_REFLECTIONS                 = Sky Reflections
option.SKY_REFLECTIONS.comment              = Makes water and shiny blocks reflect the sky. Enhances the blue sky reflection on water surfaces for a more realistic appearance.
option.SSR_ROUGHNESS_SUPPORT           = Roughness Support
option.SSR_ROUGHNESS_SUPPORT.comment        = Makes reflections on rough surfaces appear properly rough. Without this, rough surfaces appear mirror-like. Significant performance impact.
option.SSR_RAY_COUNT                   = Ray Count
option.SSR_RAY_COUNT.comment              = Reflection rays per pixel. More rays mean less noise at higher cost.
option.SSR_INTERSECTION_STEPS_SMOOTH   = Intersection Steps - Smooth
option.SSR_INTERSECTION_STEPS_SMOOTH.comment    = Intersection-test count for smooth reflections. Higher is more accurate but slower.
option.SSR_INTERSECTION_STEPS_ROUGH    = Intersection Steps - Rough
option.SSR_INTERSECTION_STEPS_ROUGH.comment = Adjusts the accuracy of rough reflections. Higher values improve quality but reduce performance. Controls intersection tests for non-mirror-like surfaces.
option.SSR_REFINEMENT_STEPS            = Refinement Steps
option.SSR_REFINEMENT_STEPS.comment       = Adjusts the refinement quality for all reflections. Higher values improve accuracy but increase performance cost. Final polishing step for reflections.
option.SSR_ROUGHNESS_THRESHOLD         = Roughness Threshold
option.SSR_ROUGHNESS_THRESHOLD.comment      = Adjusts the roughness threshold for reflections. Lower values reflect on rougher surfaces, higher values only reflect on smooth/mirror-like surfaces.

# Water settings

option.WATER_CAUSTICS                  = Water Caustics
option.WATER_CAUSTICS.comment               = Dancing light patterns beneath the water surface. Created by light refracting through water waves. Best visible with brighter sunlight.
option.WATER_CAUSTICS_INTENSITY        = Water Caustics Intensity
option.WATER_CAUSTICS_INTENSITY.comment = Controls water caustics intensity.
option.RAIN_RIPPLES                    = Rain Ripples
option.RAIN_RIPPLES.comment            = Expanding raindrop ripple rings on still, sky-exposed water. Costs one texture sample per water texel.
option.RAIN_RIPPLE_STRENGTH            = Rain Ripple Strength
option.RAIN_RIPPLE_STRENGTH.comment    = Adjusts how strongly rain ripples distort the water surface normal. Higher = more pronounced, choppier ripples.
option.WATER_CAUSTICS.comment          = Adjust the brightness of water caustics
option.WATER_EDGE_HIGHLIGHT            = Water Edge Highlight
option.WATER_EDGE_HIGHLIGHT.comment       = White highlights at the water surface edge. Makes water boundaries more visible against terrain, especially in shallow water.
option.WATER_EDGE_HIGHLIGHT_INTENSITY  = Water Edge Highlight Intensity
option.WATER_EDGE_HIGHLIGHT_INTENSITY.comment = Controls water edge highlight intensity.
option.SNELLS_WINDOW                   = Snell's Window
option.SNELLS_WINDOW.comment           = Total internal reflection underwater
option.WATER_TEXTURE                   = Water Texture
option.WATER_TEXTURE.comment              = Controls water texture rendering mode. Off: no texture. Highlights: adds RTX-style highlights. Vanilla: uses standard Minecraft water texture.
option.BIOME_WATER_COLOR               = Biome-Colored Water
option.BIOME_WATER_COLOR.comment       = Water absorption takes the biome water colour into account

value.WATER_TEXTURE.WATER_TEXTURE_OFF                   = Off
value.WATER_TEXTURE.WATER_TEXTURE_HIGHLIGHT             = Highlights
value.WATER_TEXTURE.WATER_TEXTURE_VANILLA               = Vanilla
value.WATER_TEXTURE.WATER_TEXTURE_HIGHLIGHT_UNDERGROUND = Highlights (Underground only)

option.WATER_WAVES                     = Enabled
option.WATER_WAVES.comment = Controls water wave animation. Enables the flowing water effect with procedural wave patterns. Significant performance impact with high iteration counts.
option.WATER_WAVE_ITERATIONS           = Iterations
option.WATER_WAVE_ITERATIONS.comment = Controls iterations.
option.WATER_WAVE_STRENGTH             = Intensity
option.WATER_WAVE_STRENGTH.comment = Controls intensity.
option.WATER_WAVE_FREQUENCY            = Frequency
option.WATER_WAVE_FREQUENCY.comment = Controls frequency.
option.WATER_WAVE_SPEED_STILL          = Speed (Still)
option.WATER_WAVE_SPEED_STILL.comment = Controls speed (still).
option.WATER_WAVE_SPEED_FLOWING        = Speed (Flowing)
option.WATER_WAVE_SPEED_FLOWING.comment = Controls speed (flowing).
option.WATER_WAVE_PERSISTENCE          = Persistence
option.WATER_WAVE_PERSISTENCE.comment = Controls persistence.
option.WATER_WAVE_LACUNARITY           = Lacunarity
option.WATER_WAVE_LACUNARITY.comment = Controls lacunarity.
option.WATER_PARALLAX                  = Water Parallax
option.WATER_PARALLAX.comment          = Makes water waves appear three-dimensional by offsetting texture coordinates based on view angle. Creates depth effect in water. Performance impact moderate.
option.WATER_DISPLACEMENT              = Water Displacement
option.WATER_DISPLACEMENT.comment        = Gently waves water geometry for shoreline movement and a less flat surface. Minimal cost.
option.WATER_WAVES_HEIGHT_VARIATION           = Local Height Variation 
option.WATER_WAVES_HEIGHT_VARIATION.comment   = Controls local height variation of water waves. Makes wave heights vary across the surface for a more natural, organic appearance.

option.WATER_ABSORPTION_R              = §c▍ §fRed Absorption
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_R.comment         = Controls the red absorption color channel underwater. Determines how much red light is absorbed, affecting the blue/green tint of water.
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_G              = §a▍ §fGreen Absorption
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_G.comment         = Green light absorption underwater. Balances with red absorption for natural water color.
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_B              = §9▍ §fBlue Absorption
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_B.comment         = Blue light absorption underwater. Works with red and green for the characteristic water color.
option.WATER_SCATTERING                = Scattering
option.WATER_SCATTERING.comment           = Controls light scattering within water. Affects how light penetrates and spreads through the water column, influencing overall water brightness and color.

option.WATER_ABSORPTION_R_UNDERWATER   = §c▍ §fRed Absorption - Underwater
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_R_UNDERWATER.comment = Controls the red absorption color channel when underwater. Overrides surface absorption for underwater view.
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_G_UNDERWATER   = §a▍ §fGreen Absorption - Underwater
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_G_UNDERWATER.comment = Controls the green absorption color channel when underwater. Complements red absorption for realistic underwater coloring.
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_B_UNDERWATER   = §9▍ §fBlue Absorption - Underwater
option.WATER_ABSORPTION_B_UNDERWATER.comment = Controls the blue absorption color channel when underwater. Final component in creating the complete underwater color palette.
option.WATER_SCATTERING_UNDERWATER     = Scattering - Underwater
option.WATER_SCATTERING_UNDERWATER.comment     = Controls light scattering when underwater. Determines how light spreads and penetrates the water column for the submerged view.

# Post-processing settings

option.BLOOM                           = Bloom
option.BLOOM.comment                    = Soft glow effect around bright areas and light sources. Simulates camera lens flare and bright light bleeding. Performance impact varies with intensity.
option.BLOOM_INTENSITY                 = Bloom Intensity
option.BLOOM_INTENSITY.comment          = Adjusts the bloom intensity. Higher values increase the glow effect and area affected, but may reduce performance.
option.BLOOM_SPREAD                    = Bloom Spread
option.BLOOM_UPSAMPLING_FILTER         = Bloom Filter
option.BLOOM_UPSAMPLING_FILTER.comment = Selects the bloom upsampling filter mode or method.
value.BLOOM_UPSAMPLING_FILTER.texture  = Bilinear
value.BLOOM_UPSAMPLING_FILTER.bicubic_filter = Bicubic
option.BLOOM_SPREAD.comment            = Adjusts how much the bloom spreads out
option.DOF                             = Depth of field
option.DOF.comment                       = Camera depth of field effect. Blurs areas outside the focal distance to simulate camera optics. Controls how much of the scene is in focus.
option.CHROMATIC_DISPERSION            = Chromatic Dispersion
option.CHROMATIC_DISPERSION.comment      = Radial spectral fringing scaled by defocus, simulating real camera lens dispersion. In-focus regions stay clean; blurred areas fringe with color.
option.CHROMATIC_DISPERSION_STRENGTH   = Dispersion Strength
option.CHROMATIC_DISPERSION_STRENGTH.comment = Adjusts the strength of the chromatic dispersion fringing. Higher values widen the red/blue separation in out-of-focus areas.
option.DOF_SAMPLES                     = DoF Samples
option.DOF_SAMPLES.comment               = Number of samples for depth of field calculation. Higher values produce a smoother blur but increase performance cost.
option.DOF_FOCUS                       = DoF Focus
option.DOF_MAX_RADIUS                  = DoF Max Radius
option.DOF_MAX_RADIUS.comment             = Caps the circle of confusion as a fraction of screen height. Lower values keep backgrounds sharper and save performance; higher values allow creamier blur.
option.DOF_FOCUS.comment                 = Focal distance for depth of field. Controls the distance from the camera that appears in focus. Objects closer or further than this distance will be blurred.
option.MOTION_BLUR                     = Motion Blur
option.MOTION_BLUR.comment                = Cinematic motion blur effect. Simulates camera shutter speed. Helpful for smoothing low framerates but can cause motion sickness in some users.
option.MOTION_BLUR_SAMPLES             = Motion Blur Samples
option.MOTION_BLUR_SAMPLES.comment        = Number of samples along the motion trail. Higher values give smoother streaks at higher GPU cost.
option.MOTION_BLUR_SCALE               = Motion Blur Scale
option.MOTION_BLUR_SCALE.comment          = Artistic multiplier on the shutter-driven trail length. Shutter speed sets the physical baseline; this scales it.
option.LENS_FLARE                      = Lens Flare
option.LENS_FLARE.comment                 = Ghosts, halo and anamorphic streak from bright lights scattering inside the lens. Computed pre-tonemap so flare grades with the scene.
option.LENS_FLARE_HALO                 = Flare Halo
option.LENS_FLARE_HALO.comment            = Halo ring around the sun on top of the ghost chain.
option.LENS_FLARE_INTENSITY            = Flare Intensity
option.LENS_FLARE_INTENSITY.comment       = Overall strength of ghosts, halo and streak.
option.LENS_FLARE_THRESHOLD            = Flare Threshold
option.LENS_FLARE_THRESHOLD.comment       = Scene luminance above which highlights seed flare. Lower values let lamps and glints flare; higher isolates the sun.
option.LENS_FLARE_GHOSTS               = Ghost Count
option.LENS_FLARE_GHOSTS.comment          = Number of ghosts strung along the sun axis. More ghosts cost performance.
option.LENS_FLARE_SPACING              = Ghost Spacing
option.LENS_FLARE_SPACING.comment         = Spacing of the ghost chain along the sun-to-center axis.
option.LENS_FLARE_HALO_RADIUS          = Halo Radius
option.LENS_FLARE_HALO_RADIUS.comment     = Radius of the halo ring around the sun.
option.LENS_FLARE_HALO_WIDTH           = Halo Width
option.LENS_FLARE_HALO_WIDTH.comment      = Thickness of the halo ring.
option.CAM_SENSOR_WIDTH                = Sensor Width
option.CAM_SENSOR_WIDTH.comment           = Camera sensor width in millimetres. Larger sensors give shallower depth of field at the same aperture.
option.CAM_FSTOPS                      = Aperture F-Stops
option.CAM_FSTOPS.comment                 = Lens aperture. Low values (f/0.8) give razor-thin focus; high values (f/16) keep the scene sharp deep into the distance.
option.CAM_SHUTTER_SPEED               = Shutter Speed
option.CAM_SHUTTER_SPEED.comment          = Camera shutter speed as 1/N seconds. Slower speeds streak motion blur longer; 1/60 matches the old neutral look.
option.CAM_ISO                         = ISO Sensitivity
option.CAM_ISO.comment                    = Sensor sensitivity. Doubling ISO doubles exposure brightness across manual and auto exposure alike.
option.CAM_EXPOSURE_COMPENSATION       = Exposure Compensation
option.CAM_EXPOSURE_COMPENSATION.comment   = EV compensation dial for the exposure triangle. Brightens or darkens around the aperture/shutter/ISO result, like aperture-priority mode on a real camera.
option.TAA                             = TAA
option.TAA.comment                     = Temporal anti-aliasing over multiple frames. Reduces flicker but can ghost on fast motion. Required for TAAU.
option.FXAA                            = FXAA Pass
option.FXAA.comment                    = Fast approximate anti-aliasing. Softens edges and reduces aliasing with minimal performance impact. Works in conjunction with TAA to improve motion clarity.
option.TAAU                            = TAA Upscaling
option.TAAU.comment                    = Renders below native resolution and upscales with TAA. Much faster, with some loss of sharpness and stability.
option.TAAU_RENDER_SCALE               = TAAU Render Scale
option.TAAU_RENDER_SCALE.comment       = Internal render resolution for TAA upscaling, as a fraction of screen size. Lower is faster but softer.
option.CAS                             = Image Sharpening
option.CAS.comment                     = Contrast-adaptive sharpening. Sharpens the final image to recover detail lost from anti-aliasing. Adjust intensity to avoid halo artifacts.
option.CAS_INTENSITY                   = Image Sharpening Intensity
option.CAS_INTENSITY.comment           = Adjusts the strength of the contrast-adaptive sharpening effect. Higher values increase detail but may introduce halo artifacts.
option.VIGNETTE                        = Vignette
option.VIGNETTE.comment                 = Darkens the edges of the screen (vignetting effect). Simulates camera lens natural darkening at the corners.
option.VIGNETTE_INTENSITY              = Vignette Intensity
option.VIGNETTE_INTENSITY.comment         = Adjusts the intensity of the vignette effect. Higher values increase the darkening at screen edges.
option.VIGNETTE_START                  = Vignette Start
option.VIGNETTE_START.comment             = Radial distance from screen center where the vignette falloff begins.
option.VIGNETTE_END                    = Vignette End
option.VIGNETTE_END.comment               = Radial distance where the vignette reaches full strength.
option.VIGNETTE_EXPONENT                 = Vignette Rolloff
option.VIGNETTE_EXPONENT.comment          = Shapes the vignette falloff curve. Higher values concentrate darkening toward the corners.

value.DOF_FOCUS.-1.0                   = Automatic

option.tonemap                         = Tonemap Operator
option.tonemap.comment                 = Tonemapping operator. Shapes highlights, brightness and overall contrast.

value.tonemap.tonemap_aces_fit         = ACES Fit
value.tonemap.tonemap_aces_full        = ACES Full
value.tonemap.tonemap_hejl_2015        = Hejl 2015
value.tonemap.tonemap_hejl_burgess     = Hejl-Burgess
value.tonemap.tonemap_lottes           = Lottes
value.tonemap.tonemap_uncharted_2      = Uncharted 2
value.tonemap.tonemap_tech             = Tech
value.tonemap.tonemap_ozius            = Ozius
value.tonemap.tonemap_reinhard         = Reinhard
value.tonemap.tonemap_reinhard_jodie   = Reinhard-Jodie
value.tonemap.tonemap_agx              = AGX
value.tonemap.tonemap_agx_punchy       = AGX Punchy
value.tonemap.tonemap_agx_golden       = AGX Golden

# Color Grading

option.GRADE_BRIGHTNESS                = Brightness
option.GRADE_BRIGHTNESS.comment        = Pre-tonemap scene brightness. A global exposure trim applied after lighting.
option.GRADE_CONTRAST                  = Contrast
option.GRADE_CONTRAST.comment          = Tonal range around the pivot. Above 1.0 deepens darks and brightens brights; below 1.0 flattens toward grey.
option.GRADE_PIVOT                     = Contrast Pivot
option.GRADE_PIVOT.comment             = Luminance anchor for contrast (0–1 linear). 0.18 is photographic middle grey.
option.GRADE_SATURATION                = Saturation
option.GRADE_SATURATION.comment        = Uniform chroma scale in Oklab space, so hues stay stable. 0.0 is greyscale.
option.GRADE_VIBRANCE                  = Vibrance
option.GRADE_VIBRANCE.comment          = Gentle saturation for muted colors only. Lifts dull areas without oversaturating vivid ones; negatives mute vivid areas.
option.GRADE_WHITE_BALANCE             = White Balance
option.GRADE_WHITE_BALANCE.comment     = Image color temperature. 6500 K is neutral daylight; lower is cooler, higher is warmer.
option.GRADE_LIFT_R                    = §c▍ §fShadow Lift — Red
option.GRADE_LIFT_R.comment            = Raises or lowers the red channel in the darkest parts of the image (shadows/blacks). Positive = warm shadows, negative = cool shadows.
option.GRADE_LIFT_G                    = §a▍ §fShadow Lift — Green
option.GRADE_LIFT_G.comment            = Raises or lowers the green channel in shadows. Combine with red and blue lift to tint the darkest tones any color.
option.GRADE_LIFT_B                    = §9▍ §fShadow Lift — Blue
option.GRADE_LIFT_B.comment            = Raises or lowers the blue channel in shadows. Positive = blue-tinted blacks, negative = yellow-tinted blacks.
option.GRADE_GAMMA_R                   = §c▍ §fMidtone Gamma — Red
option.GRADE_GAMMA_R.comment           = Power-curve adjustment for the red channel in midtones. Above 1.0 brightens reds in the middle range; below 1.0 darkens them.
option.GRADE_GAMMA_G                   = §a▍ §fMidtone Gamma — Green
option.GRADE_GAMMA_G.comment           = Power-curve adjustment for the green channel in midtones. Useful for shifting the overall midtone hue toward magenta or green.
option.GRADE_GAMMA_B                   = §9▍ §fMidtone Gamma — Blue
option.GRADE_GAMMA_B.comment           = Power-curve adjustment for the blue channel in midtones. Above 1.0 adds a cool blue cast to midtones.
option.GRADE_GAIN_R                    = §c▍ §fHighlight Gain — Red
option.GRADE_GAIN_R.comment            = Multiplies the red channel in the brightest parts of the image. Above 1.0 warms highlights; below 1.0 cools them.
option.GRADE_GAIN_G                    = §a▍ §fHighlight Gain — Green
option.GRADE_GAIN_G.comment            = Multiplies the green channel in highlights. Combine with red and blue gain to tint the brightest tones.
option.GRADE_GAIN_B                    = §9▍ §fHighlight Gain — Blue
option.GRADE_GAIN_B.comment            = Multiplies the blue channel in highlights. Positive = cool blue highlights, negative = warm yellow highlights.
option.GRADE_OKLAB_PIVOT               = Perceptual Contrast Pivot
option.GRADE_OKLAB_PIVOT.comment       = The lightness value in Oklab space (0–1) that stays fixed when the perceptual contrast slider is applied. 0.5 = perceptual midpoint.
option.GRADE_OKLAB_CONTRAST            = Perceptual Contrast
option.GRADE_OKLAB_CONTRAST.comment    = Perceptual contrast in Oklab space. Preserves hue in saturated areas, unlike linear contrast.
option.GRADE_SHADOW_LOW                = Shadow Range — Low
option.GRADE_SHADOW_LOW.comment        = The lower luminance boundary of the shadow tonal range used by the three-way color wheel. Pixels below this value are fully in the shadow zone.
option.GRADE_SHADOW_HIGH               = Shadow Range — High
option.GRADE_SHADOW_HIGH.comment       = The upper luminance boundary of the shadow zone. Pixels between Shadow Low and Shadow High blend between shadow and midtone color wheels.
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_LOW             = Highlight Range — Low
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_LOW.comment     = The lower luminance boundary of the highlight zone. Pixels between Highlight Low and Highlight High blend between midtone and highlight color wheels.
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_HIGH            = Highlight Range — High
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_HIGH.comment    = The upper luminance boundary of the highlight zone. Pixels above this value are fully in the highlight zone.
option.GRADE_SHADOW_STRENGTH           = Shadow Tint Strength
option.GRADE_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment   = How strongly the shadow color wheel hue is applied to dark areas. 0 = no tint, 1 = full tint at the chosen shadow hue and saturation.
option.GRADE_MID_STRENGTH              = Midtone Tint Strength
option.GRADE_MID_STRENGTH.comment      = How strongly the midtone color wheel hue is applied to middle-luminance areas.
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_STRENGTH        = Highlight Tint Strength
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment = How strongly the highlight color wheel hue is applied to bright areas.
option.GRADE_SHADOW_HUE                = Shadow Hue
option.GRADE_SHADOW_HUE.comment        = The hue angle (0–360°) of the color tint applied to shadows when Shadow Tint Strength > 0. 220° = cool blue-purple, 30° = warm orange.
option.GRADE_MID_HUE                   = Midtone Hue
option.GRADE_MID_HUE.comment           = The hue angle of the color tint applied to midtones when Midtone Tint Strength > 0.
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_HUE             = Highlight Hue
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_HUE.comment     = The hue angle of the color tint applied to highlights when Highlight Tint Strength > 0. 45° = warm golden highlights.
option.GRADE_SHADOW_TINT_HUE           = Shadow Tint Hue
option.GRADE_SHADOW_TINT_HUE.comment   = Hue angle for the dedicated shadow tint pass (separate from the three-way wheel). Lets you add a subtle color cast to just the darkest tones.
option.GRADE_SHADOW_TINT_SAT           = Shadow Tint Saturation
option.GRADE_SHADOW_TINT_SAT.comment   = Saturation of the dedicated shadow tint. 0 = no tint, 1 = fully saturated shadow cast at the chosen hue.
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_TINT_HUE        = Highlight Tint Hue
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_TINT_HUE.comment = Hue angle for the dedicated highlight tint pass. Adds a color cast to only the brightest parts of the image.
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_TINT_SAT        = Highlight Tint Saturation
option.GRADE_HIGHLIGHT_TINT_SAT.comment = Saturation of the dedicated highlight tint. 0 = no tint, 1 = fully saturated highlight cast.
option.GRADE_ORANGE_SAT_BOOST          = §6▍ §fOrange Saturation
option.GRADE_ORANGE_SAT_BOOST.comment  = Saturation for oranges (~15–45°): sunsets, skin, autumn foliage. Negatives mute toward grey.
option.GRADE_TEAL_SAT_BOOST            = §b▍ §fTeal Saturation
option.GRADE_TEAL_SAT_BOOST.comment    = Selectively boosts or cuts saturation in the teal/cyan hue range (~165–210°). Positive = more vivid water and sky reflections. Negative = desaturates teals.
option.GRADE_GREEN_SAT_BOOST           = §a▍ §fGreen Saturation
option.GRADE_GREEN_SAT_BOOST.comment   = Selectively boosts or cuts saturation in the green hue range (~75–150°). Positive = more vivid foliage and grass. Negative = desaturates greens toward olive.
option.GRADE_GREEN_HUE_SHIFT           = §a▍ §fGreen Hue Shift
option.GRADE_GREEN_HUE_SHIFT.comment   = Rotates greens up to ±20°. Positive toward yellow-green, negative toward teal.
option.GRADE_SELECTIVE_BLEND           = Selective Grade Blend
option.GRADE_SELECTIVE_BLEND.comment   = Master blend weight for all selective color adjustments (orange/teal/green saturation and green hue shift). 0 = no selective grading, 1 = full effect.
option.GRADE_BLACK_POINT               = Black Point
option.GRADE_BLACK_POINT.comment       = Raises the minimum output level, lifting blacks toward grey. Useful for a faded/matte look or to match a display with elevated black levels. 0 = true black.
option.GRADE_WHITE_POINT               = White Point
option.GRADE_WHITE_POINT.comment       = Lowers the maximum output level, compressing highlights toward grey. Useful for a filmic, low-contrast look. 0 = full white.
suffix.GRADE_WHITE_BALANCE             = K
suffix.GRADE_GREEN_HUE_SHIFT           = °

option.PURKINJE_SHIFT                  = Purkinje Shift
option.PURKINJE_SHIFT.comment          = Purkinje effect: night vision shifts toward blue-green sensitivity with desaturated colors.
option.PURKINJE_SHIFT_INTENSITY        = Purkinje Shift Intensity
option.PURKINJE_SHIFT_INTENSITY.comment = Controls the strength of the Purkinje effect. Higher values increase the shift toward blue-green sensitivity and desaturation in low light.
option.PURKINJE_SHIFT_R                = §c▍ §fPurkinje Response — Red
option.PURKINJE_SHIFT_R.comment         = Red channel weight of the scotopic tint. Lower values push night vision cooler.
option.PURKINJE_SHIFT_G                = §a▍ §fPurkinje Response — Green
option.PURKINJE_SHIFT_G.comment         = Green channel weight of the scotopic tint. Rods peak in blue-green, so this dominates the night hue.
option.PURKINJE_SHIFT_B                = §9▍ §fPurkinje Response — Blue
option.PURKINJE_SHIFT_B.comment         = Blue channel weight of the scotopic tint. Higher values deepen the classic blue night shift.

# Exposure

option.AUTO_EXPOSURE                         = Auto Exposure
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE.comment = Enables advanced global auto exposure. Automatically adjusts exposure based on scene brightness.

option.LOCAL_EXPOSURE                         = Local Exposure
option.LOCAL_EXPOSURE.comment                 = Applies spatially adaptive HDR exposure while preserving the global exposure and protecting highlight and shadow detail.
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_MIN                     = Minimum Exposure
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_MIN.comment             = Sets the minimum exposure limit. Prevents the image from becoming too bright in bright scenes.
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_MAX                     = Maximum Exposure
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_MAX.comment             = Sets the maximum exposure limit. Prevents the image from becoming too dark in dark scenes.
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_RATE_DIM_TO_BRIGHT      = Adaptation Speed — Brightening
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_RATE_DIM_TO_BRIGHT.comment = Adjusts how quickly exposure adapts when the scene gets brighter (e.g., looking from a cave to the sky). Higher = faster adaptation.
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_RATE_BRIGHT_TO_DIM      = Adaptation Speed — Darkening
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_RATE_BRIGHT_TO_DIM.comment = Adjusts how quickly exposure adapts when the scene gets darker (e.g., entering a cave). Higher = faster dimming.
option.MANUAL_EXPOSURE_VALUE                 = Manual Exposure Value
option.MANUAL_EXPOSURE_VALUE.comment        = Manually set the exposure value. Overrides auto exposure settings.
option.MANUAL_EXPOSURE_USE_SCREEN_BRIGHTNESS = Use Brightness Slider
option.MANUAL_EXPOSURE_USE_SCREEN_BRIGHTNESS.comment = Exposure value interpolates between minimum and maximum based on the Brightness slider in Video Settings.
option.HISTOGRAM_BINS                        = Histogram Bins
option.HISTOGRAM_BINS.comment                = Controls the number of histogram bins used for exposure calculation. More bins provide more precise exposure adjustment.
option.HISTOGRAM_TARGET                      = Histogram Target CDF Value
option.HISTOGRAM_TARGET.comment              = Controls the target brightness for auto exposure using the histogram method. Higher values produce a brighter image.
option.HISTOGRAM_SHADOW_WEIGHT               = Meter Shadow Weight
option.HISTOGRAM_SHADOW_WEIGHT.comment       = Weight of the shadow population in the three-population exposure meter. Higher values protect shadow detail from crushing.
option.HISTOGRAM_HIGHLIGHT_WEIGHT            = Meter Highlight Weight
option.HISTOGRAM_HIGHLIGHT_WEIGHT.comment    = Weight of the highlight population in the exposure meter. Higher values protect bright areas like sunsets from blowing out.
option.LOCAL_EXPOSURE_REGIONAL               = Local Regional Blend
option.LOCAL_EXPOSURE_REGIONAL.comment       = Blends the fine bilateral correction toward area-scale dodge and burn. Higher values adapt whole regions; 0 keeps pixel-local detail only.
option.LOCAL_EXPOSURE_RANGE                  = Local Regional Range
option.LOCAL_EXPOSURE_RANGE.comment          = Maximum exposure shift in stops the regional adaptation may apply. Caps grading so it never overrides global exposure.
option.LOCAL_EXPOSURE_DETAIL                 = Local Detail Strength
option.LOCAL_EXPOSURE_DETAIL.comment         = Scales the fine bilateral detail correction. Lower values leave only the area-scale regional grading.


