screen.academy_color                    = Academy Color
option.COLOR_GRADING                    = Color Grading
option.COLOR_GRADING.comment            = Full color grading pipeline: brightness, contrast, white balance, ASC CDL, Oklab contrast, selective hues and tints. Off passes tonemapper output through.
option.ACADEMY_EXPOSURE                 = ACES Exposure
option.ACADEMY_EXPOSURE.comment         = Pre-tonemap exposure in stops for ACES. Shifts highlight rolloff without changing overall brightness.
option.ACADEMY_CONTRAST                = ACES Contrast
option.ACADEMY_CONTRAST.comment        = ACES S-curve steepness. Above 1.0 punches blacks and highlights; below 1.0 softens.
option.ACADEMY_SATURATION              = ACES Saturation
option.ACADEMY_SATURATION.comment      = Chroma inside ACES before the final curve. Saturated highlights still compress naturally.
option.ACADEMY_HIGHLIGHT_ROLLOFF       = ACES Highlight Rolloff
option.ACADEMY_HIGHLIGHT_ROLLOFF.comment = ACES highlight compression past middle grey. Higher is softer with more detail; lower clips harder.
option.ACADEMY_SHADOW_TOE              = ACES Shadow Toe
option.ACADEMY_SHADOW_TOE.comment      = Lifts the bottom of the ACES curve, preventing pure black and adding a subtle shadow lift. Higher = more lifted blacks with visible shadow detail, filmic look.
option.ACADEMY_COLORFULNESS            = ACES Colorfulness
option.ACADEMY_COLORFULNESS.comment    = ACES vividness shift. Positive adds midtone chroma without touching luminance.
option.ACADEMY_RRT_EXPOSURE            = ACES RRT Exposure
option.ACADEMY_RRT_EXPOSURE.comment    = Exposure in stops before the RRT. Moves the scene along the filmic S-curve itself.
option.ACADEMY_RRT_GLOW                = ACES RRT Glow
option.ACADEMY_RRT_GLOW.comment        = RRT glow lifting dim saturated colors. Higher means dreamier highlights; 0.10 is default.
option.ACADEMY_RRT_SAT                 = ACES RRT Saturation
option.ACADEMY_RRT_SAT.comment         = Global desaturation inside the RRT sweeteners. Lower = more filmic muted response before the tonescale. 0.96 matches the reference fit.
option.ACADEMY_ODT_SAT                 = ACES ODT Saturation
option.ACADEMY_ODT_SAT.comment         = Desaturation in the output device transform compensating luminance differences. Lower tames oversaturated brights after the tonescale.
option.ACADEMY_RRT_GAMMA               = ACES RRT Gamma
option.ACADEMY_RRT_GAMMA.comment       = Gamma shaping applied inside the RRT before the tonescale. Above 1.0 darkens midtones into the curve, below 1.0 lifts them.
option.ACADEMY_RRT_RED                 = ACES RRT Red Modifier
option.ACADEMY_RRT_RED.comment         = Strength of the RRT red modifier that pulls red hues toward the pivot. Higher = stronger classic ACES red rendering. 1.0 is the pack default.
option.ACADEMY_CONTRAST_PIVOT          = ACES Contrast Pivot
option.ACADEMY_CONTRAST_PIVOT.comment  = Middle-grey anchor for ACES contrast. 0.18 is reference 18% grey.
option.AGX_EXPOSURE                    = AGX Exposure
option.AGX_EXPOSURE.comment            = Pre-tonemap exposure offset in stops fed into the AGX curve. +1 = twice as bright entering the curve. Shifts where highlights begin to compress.
option.AGX_CONTRAST                    = AGX Contrast
option.AGX_CONTRAST.comment            = AGX S-curve slope. Above 1.0 adds punch; below 1.0 flattens. Kinder to saturated highlights than ACES.
option.AGX_SATURATION                  = AGX Saturation
option.AGX_SATURATION.comment          = Chroma inside AGX before the curve. Gamut compression rolls saturated colors off smoothly.
option.AGX_HIGHLIGHT_ROLLOFF           = AGX Highlight Rolloff
option.AGX_HIGHLIGHT_ROLLOFF.comment   = AGX highlight compression toward white. Higher is softer with more detail; lower is harder.
option.AGX_PUNCH                      = AGX Punch
option.AGX_PUNCH.comment               = Midtone contrast and saturation boost. Positive adds pop; negative goes muted and filmic.
option.AGX_GOLDEN                     = AGX Golden
option.AGX_GOLDEN.comment              = Shifts the AGX output toward a warm golden tint. Positive = warmer, more cinematic golden grade. Negative = cooler, more neutral or bluish output.
option.AGX_SHADOW_TOE                  = AGX Shadow Toe
option.AGX_SHADOW_TOE.comment          = Lifts the bottom of the AGX curve, the mirror of highlight rolloff for shadows. Higher = more lifted blacks with visible shadow detail, filmic look.
option.AGX_HIGHLIGHT_DESAT             = AGX Highlight Desat
option.AGX_HIGHLIGHT_DESAT.comment     = Desaturates highlights toward neutral grey above the shoulder. Higher = more filmic white clipping on bright saturated sources instead of colored clipping.
option.AGX_CONTRAST_PIVOT              = AGX Contrast Pivot
option.AGX_CONTRAST_PIVOT.comment      = Middle-grey anchor for AGX contrast. 0.18 is reference 18% grey.

